---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import bgImage from '../../assets/banner/loading-background.png';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const optimizedBg = await getImage({ src: bgImage, width: 1672, format: 'webp' });
---
<Layout title="About" lang="en" switchHref={`${base}about/`} pageBackgroundSrc={optimizedBg.src}>
  <h1>About Vantaari</h1>
  <p>
    Vantaari is a single-player 4X space game in the style of EVE Online:
    exploration, industry, trade, and combat across a persistent galaxy where
    your actions have real consequences for territory, economy, and power.
    Nothing scripted, all of it emergent.
  </p>

  <h2>The universe</h2>
  <p>The galaxy is divided between several factions, each with its own identity:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Nova Union.</strong> Order, industry, and security.</li>
    <li><strong>Helios Concord.</strong> Diplomacy, science, and civil defense. Allied with Nova Union.</li>
    <li><strong>Freehold League.</strong> Free stations and independent trade.</li>
    <li><strong>Veyra Syndicate.</strong> Corporations, markets, and technology.</li>
    <li><strong>Khar Dominion.</strong> Militarism, frontier, and conquest.</li>
    <li><strong>Redwake Raiders.</strong> Crime, plunder, and smuggling.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Current features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Explore a solar system and a galactic map connecting several systems.</li>
    <li>Travel in warp for longer distances.</li>
    <li>Mine asteroids for raw minerals.</li>
    <li>An economic simulation: minerals get refined into materials and components through refineries, factories, and markets.</li>
    <li>Fit and swap weapons, shields, and other modules on your ship.</li>
    <li>Real combat: weapons, shields, hull damage, and ships that can be destroyed.</li>
    <li>Enemies that attack and defend themselves on their own.</li>
    <li>Drones you can launch from your ship.</li>
    <li>Bounty hunting against wanted pirates.</li>
    <li>Characters with dialogue, voices, and branching conversations.</li>
    <li>An in-game codex with info about the setting.</li>
    <li>Multiple camera modes: orbital, tactical, and first-person.</li>
    <li>Full sound design: engines, weapons, warp, and music.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What's coming</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Deeper diplomacy between factions.</li>
    <li>Missions with real objectives and rewards.</li>
    <li>Trade missions.</li>
    <li>Transport missions.</li>
    <li>Careers.</li>
    <li>A technology research system.</li>
    <li>Fleet command, to coordinate multiple ships at once.</li>
    <li>More station types and a more dynamic economy.</li>
  </ul>
</Layout>
